      "id": "R7-FIX-RUNTIME-002",
      "priority": 2,
      "status": "fixed",
      "file": "src/runtime/dev-resources.ts",
      "originalLine": 45,
      "title": "Plugin preview enumerated a whole directory before applying resource limits",
      "trigger": "An authenticated development plugin preview points to a wide real directory. Before this change readdir materialized and sorted the entire names array before the first file-count check.",
      "impact": "The nominal 512-file/1024-directory budget did not bound directory-list allocation or sorting work. Small-resource reproduction observed a real 2048-entry returned array before capacity rejection; no out-of-memory result is claimed.",
      "evidence": {
        "baselineSourceSha256": "d81709a2640a354737abc0fe0231e5cbcd93c7ce48f4cbdf3e244a4d4a686396",
        "realEmptyFiles": 2048,
        "observedNamesArrayLength": 2048,
        "failedRegression": ".work/test-results/run-UERjBv/vitest.json",
        "assertion": "expected 2048 to be less than or equal to 1536"
      },
      "fix": "Use opendir with a 32-entry internal buffer, count actual entries across the whole tree before retaining names, reject the first entry beyond 1535, close handles in finally, and sort only bounded names to preserve traversal order and hash behavior. Original round7 evidence was not changed."
    }
  ],
